# 
# https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000228> .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "control assessment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "évaluation d'une mesure de sécurité"@fr .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "control test"@en .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A planned act in which an assessor tests or reviews a control measure of an organisation at a stated date, over a stated scope and by a stated procedure, and records its result and the evidence gathered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Acte planifié par lequel un évaluateur teste ou examine une mesure de sécurité d'une organisation à une date, sur un périmètre et selon une procédure donnés, et en consigne le résultat et les preuves recueillies."@fr .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000283> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000069> .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000284> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000063> .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000285> "Specification section 5 (separate objective, implementation and assessment result): control = objective, control measure = implementation, control assessment = test."@en .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000286> "CRGO v0.8 to v1.0 Claude Implementation Specification (project owner, 2026-10-11), sections 3-13"@en .
<https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000347> <https://w3id.org/crgo/CRGO_0000286> "NIST SP 800-30 Rev. 1 (2012), Appendices D-I (threat sources, events, vulnerabilities and predisposing conditions, likelihood, impact, risk)"@en .
